1
00:00:01,200 --> 00:00:05,200


2
00:00:05,750 --> 00:00:07,671
When we think about healthy ageing,

3
00:00:07,671 --> 00:00:09,976
it is not just a question
of what we take.

4
00:00:09,976 --> 00:00:11,403
We also need to ask: when?

5
00:00:11,953 --> 00:00:14,911
Imagine you start paying
more attention to nutrition.

6
00:00:14,911 --> 00:00:18,204
You choose a supplement, and
remember to take it every day.

7
00:00:18,754 --> 00:00:21,769
But when life gets busy,
mealtimes keep changing.

8
00:00:21,769 --> 00:00:23,554
Lunch gets pushed back again.

9
00:00:24,104 --> 00:00:28,008
At night, a little more time on your
phone turns into another late bedtime.

10
00:00:28,558 --> 00:00:30,528
So, is taking a supplement enough?

11
00:00:30,528 --> 00:00:31,976
To explore that question,

12
00:00:31,976 --> 00:00:35,683
let us look inside the cell: a
city that works around the clock.

13
00:00:36,233 --> 00:00:38,359
Mitochondria are like power stations.

14
00:00:38,359 --> 00:00:41,289
They help supply the energy
cells need to function.

15
00:00:42,489 --> 00:00:46,649
Every walk, every movement, depends
on energy supplied by your cells.

16
00:00:47,199 --> 00:00:49,615
This city also has recycling centres.

17
00:00:49,615 --> 00:00:52,031
Lysosomes break down and recycle some

18
00:00:52,031 --> 00:00:54,709
damaged proteins and
cellular components.

19
00:00:55,909 --> 00:00:57,796
There is maintenance work, too.

20
00:00:57,796 --> 00:00:59,257
DNA repair, for example,

21
00:00:59,257 --> 00:01:02,970
helps cells maintain the integrity
of their genetic material.

22
00:01:04,170 --> 00:01:06,157
As we age, some energy-producing,

23
00:01:06,157 --> 00:01:09,829
clearing and maintenance functions
may become less effective.

24
00:01:09,829 --> 00:01:13,501
Damage can gradually accumulate,
potentially affecting cells,

25
00:01:13,501 --> 00:01:14,645
tissues and organs.

26
00:01:15,845 --> 00:01:18,699
But cellular activity
also follows a timetable.

27
00:01:18,699 --> 00:01:22,586
Morning light is an important
signal that helps set that timing.

28
00:01:23,136 --> 00:01:26,016
Light influences the
master clock in the brain,

29
00:01:26,016 --> 00:01:29,692
which helps coordinate clocks
in different organs and cells.

30
00:01:29,692 --> 00:01:32,204
Metabolism and some
maintenance processes

31
00:01:32,204 --> 00:01:34,349
are regulated by circadian rhythms.

32
00:01:34,349 --> 00:01:38,944
Ageing, cellular function and these
rhythms can also influence one another.

33
00:01:41,444 --> 00:01:45,043
That is why sleep and daily
rhythms deserve attention together.

34
00:01:45,043 --> 00:01:47,385
But repair does not
happen only at night.

35
00:01:47,385 --> 00:01:49,956
Different processes
follow different rhythms.

36
00:01:50,506 --> 00:01:54,765
Mealtimes can also influence some
peripheral clocks and metabolic rhythms.

37
00:01:54,765 --> 00:01:59,082
What we eat, and when we eat, are two
questions worth considering together.

38
00:02:01,582 --> 00:02:03,831
Studying an ingredient
is a little like

39
00:02:03,831 --> 00:02:06,253
studying how to improve
one power station.

40
00:02:06,253 --> 00:02:10,521
To look after the whole city, we also
need to consider the bigger picture.

41
00:02:11,071 --> 00:02:14,381
Nutrition and metabolism
provide materials and energy.

42
00:02:14,381 --> 00:02:16,465
Hormones carry regulatory signals,

43
00:02:16,465 --> 00:02:20,511
while the immune system also helps
shape the cellular environment.

44
00:02:20,511 --> 00:02:25,108
Cellular function and whole-body systems
continually influence one another.

45
00:02:26,308 --> 00:02:30,145
This is the ASCLEPIOS HEALTH
approach: a whole-system perspective,

46
00:02:30,145 --> 00:02:33,518
respect for biological rhythms,
and practical application.

47
00:02:33,518 --> 00:02:36,716
Start with the foundations
of diet, movement and sleep.

48
00:02:36,716 --> 00:02:38,634
Then consider nutritional support

49
00:02:38,634 --> 00:02:41,135
according to individual
needs and evidence.

50
00:02:41,135 --> 00:02:42,705
What to use, how to use it,

51
00:02:42,705 --> 00:02:45,670
and when to use it must be
considered individually.

52
00:02:45,670 --> 00:02:50,031
Not every supplement belongs in a fixed
morning, afternoon or evening slot.

53
00:02:50,581 --> 00:02:53,930
With ASCLEPIOS HEALTH, we
will explore cellular energy,

54
00:02:53,930 --> 00:02:55,209
recycling and repair,

55
00:02:55,209 --> 00:02:57,950
and how body functions
and biological rhythms

56
00:02:57,950 --> 00:03:00,507
can inform choices you
can make every day.

57
00:03:00,507 --> 00:03:04,831
This journey towards healthy ageing
begins with understanding yourself.

58
00:03:05,381 --> 00:03:06,365
ASCLEPIOS HEALTH.

59
00:03:06,365 --> 00:03:07,696
Starting with the cell.

60
00:03:07,696 --> 00:03:09,605
Working with the rhythms of life.
